WEBVTT

00:32:31.121 --> 00:32:35.079
Your collaboration with Amos Tversky
is obviously legendary,

00:32:35.121 --> 00:32:36.788
there's a whole Michael
Lewis book about it.

00:32:37.371 --> 00:32:41.704
Is there a lesson that you took away from
that collaboration that's informed

00:32:41.704 --> 00:32:45.996
either how you choose your collaborators
now or how you work with the people

00:32:45.996 --> 00:32:46.496
on your team?

00:32:46.788 --> 00:32:52.371
I think that one really
important thing in is.

00:32:53.663 --> 00:33:01.163
It's to be genuinely interested in what
your collaborator is say, and, you know,